## Night pillars

**Leyline Pillar.** Temporary world spawn by default: night only, 80–100 blocks from a player, every 4–6 minutes with a 50% roll, twelve-minute lifetime. Chat announces when one appears. Charge it three times with Charge Leyline (12-block range) to open a rift. Fully charged pillars go on a recharge cooldown (default 10 minutes).

## Rift encounters

A **Leyline Rift** is waves. Stay within sixty blocks or it collapses as abandoned. Die and it collapses. Clear every wave and it collapses in victory — theme loot, XP, and a 25% chance at a **Ley Crystal**.

Default encounter pool (random pick when the pillar opens):

| Encounter | Feel | Notable clear loot |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Leyline Breach | Endermen, vex, evoker | Amethyst, pearls, XP |
| Void Rift | Endermites, phantoms, shulker | Echo shards |
| Amethyst Surge | Silverfish, witches, illusioner | Budding amethyst |
| Spectral Tide | Drowned, guardians, elder guardians | Trident |
| Chaotic Echo | Creepers, blazes, ghasts | Nether star |
| Ley Storm | Breezes, vex, evoker | Heavy core |

## Crimson Thicket

<img class="wiki-shot" src="/images/leylines/crimson_thicket.jpg" alt="Crimson Thicket biome with Scarlet Aspen and Ancient Mana clusters" />

Scarlet Aspen forests with Ancient Mana growing like ore.

**Ancient Mana Cluster.** Break for 1–2 Ancient Mana. Silk touch keeps the block. This is the Nightborn’s currency.

**Scarlet Aspen.** Log, leaves, planks, sapling. The Thicket’s wood set. Saplings also sell from Nightborn for 4–8 Ancient Mana.

**Nightborn Elf.** Invisible by day unless you threaten them. Visible and trading at night. Stock: Ley Crystal for 12 Ancient Mana, two random Leyline scrolls (priced by rarity/level), and Scarlet Aspen saplings. If rift luck is cold, this is the reliable crystal source.
